       The  rraannddoomm() function uses a nonlinear additive feedback random number
       generator employing a default table of size 31 long integers to  return
       successive  pseudo‐random numbers in the range from 0 to 2^31 - 1.  The
       period of this random number generator  is  very  large,  approximately
       _1_6 _* _(_(_2_^_3_1_) _- _1_).

       The ssrraannddoomm() function sets its argument as the seed for a new sequence
       of  pseudo‐random integers to be returned by rraannddoomm().  These sequences
       are repeatable by calling ssrraannddoomm() with the same seed  value.   If  no
       seed  value  is provided, the rraannddoomm() function is automatically seeded
       with a value of 1.

